b-cardgap-2026-10-07: writer teaser-write-012", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "Almost all dolmens around the Mediterranean are oriented to a celestial feature. At the Antequera Dolmens Site, the Dolmen of Menga points instead at the nearby Peña de los Enamorados."}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: checker teaser-check-012 (check), PASS", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "almost all dolmens around the Mediterranean are oriented to a celestial feature [S5]; the Dolmen of Menga is part of the Antequera Dolmens Site [S1]; the Dolmen of Menga points instead at the nearby peak called the Peña de los Enamorados [S5]"}, {"source": "lane WB run wb-cardgap-2026-10-07: verifier teaser-verify-035 (verify), VERIFIED", "url": "output/remediation/teaser/runs/wb-cardgap-2026-10-07/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Antequera Dolmens Site is a cultural heritage ensemble of monuments in and near Antequera, Spain. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antequera_Dolmens_Site]; The Dolmen of Menga is a megalithic monument of the site. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antequera_Dolmens_Site]; Almost all dolmens around the Mediterranean are oriented to a celestial feature. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antequera_Dolmens_Site]; The Dolmen of Menga''s orientation is anomalous, i.e. it departs from the usual celestial orientation. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antequera_Dolmens_Site]; The Dolmen of Menga is oriented towards the Pena de los Enamorados. [SUPPORTED: https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/D%C3%B3lmen_de_Menga]; The Pena de los Enamorados is a nearby peak. [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Antequera_Dolmens_Site]"}]'::jsonb),
